{
  "_comment": [
    "builtin/entity hands rendering to CardItemRenderer, which draws the real card art.",
    "The display transforms below are ordinary model data - edit them and press F3+T in game",
    "to see the change without restarting.",
    "",
    "These follow vanilla's item/generated, which is what every flat item in the game uses.",
    "Note the third-person rotation is [0,0,0]: item/handheld's [0,-90,55] is a fist grip on a",
    "tool, and applying it to a flat card is what makes one look skewed and edge-on.",
    "",
    "Ground is -90 about X, not +90. The renderer draws the printed side facing +Z and the",
    "sleeve facing -Z, and rotating +90 about X sends +Z to -Y - so a card thrown on the",
    "floor landed with its face in the dirt and its sleeve up. -90 sends +Z to +Y and it",
    "lands face up, which is what dropping a card on a table does."
  ],
